From f6c3327897897ed861563d40d98b2d5cf476cfa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himanshu Joshi <himajosh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:24:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] dev_queue_xmit: Reset skb->fast_xmit flag in slow path
 transmit

Reset skb->fast_xmit flag in "dev_queue_xmit". This avoids a combination
scenarios like PPPoE with DS-Lite or other tunnels where one rule is matched
with sfe and was transmitted in fast path and the inner is transmitted through
slow path.

Change-Id: I8210f4a4eef614d22a3554fad76a388e0fc09569
Signed-off-by: Himanshu Joshi <himajosh@qti.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4229ce86284cb1145ff5a98357c1d5bd5e372298)
---
 net/core/dev.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/core/dev.c b/net/core/dev.c
index 9741433edb99..71b159be96b0 100644
--- a/net/core/dev.c
+++ b/net/core/dev.c
@@ -4957,6 +4957,12 @@ int __dev_queue_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *sb_dev)
 	skb_reset_mac_header(skb);
 	skb_assert_len(skb);
 
+	/*
+	 * if the skb landed in dev_queue_xmit then its not fast transmitted
+	 * reset this flag for further processing.
+	 */
+	skb->fast_xmit = 0;
+
 	if (unlikely(skb_shinfo(skb)->tx_flags & SKBTX_SCHED_TSTAMP))
 		__skb_tstamp_tx(skb, NULL, NULL, skb->sk, SCM_TSTAMP_SCHED);
 
-- 
